l estate investment trusts, infrastructure sector, and natural energy resources sector for its equity and fixed income investments. The firm also invests in preferred securities for its fixed income investments through its subsidiaries. The firm is a leading global investment manager specializing in real assets and alternative income, including real estate, preferred securities, infrastructure, resource equities, commodities, as well as multi-strategy solutions. Cohen & Steers, Inc. was founded in 1986 and is based in New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph M. Harvey | CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 424 people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $108K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Cohen & Steers Inc is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.7B market cap on $556M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 88% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 78-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The company is burning through $126M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +31.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 46% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 60% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.600476229659243},{"text":"Accruals elevated at +31.2% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","21 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Strengthen CNS Trial Outcomes Through Smarter Data Capture, Upcoming Webinar Hosted by Xtalks","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/strengthen-cns-trial-outcomes-through-smarter-data-capture-upcoming-webinar-hosted-by-xtalks-302937244.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794490200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.938,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cohen & Steers (CNS) Could Be 3% Overvalued After AUM Update And Property Venture","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-cns/cohen-steers/news/cohen-steers-cns-could-be-3-overvalued-after-aum-update-and","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794368169.959,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.942,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cohen & Steers Announces Changes to Realty Indexes","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/articles/cohen-steers-announces-changes-realty-002900092.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794616140.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cohen & Steers Reveals 13.36% Ownership Stake in SL Green Realty via Schedule 13G Amendment","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/cohen-steers-reveals-1336-ownership-stake-in-sl-green-realty-via-schedule-13g-amendment","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794586027.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Cohen & Steers Reveals 15.61% Ownership Stake in OUTFRONT Media","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/cohen-steers-reveals-1561-ownership-stake-in-outfront-media","date":"2026-11-13","